[h1]S3GM: Skate 3 in Gmod[/h1]
Skate 3's real skating in Garry's Mod: its own physics, flick-it tricks, grinds, manuals, bails and the mach 1 glitch, running on the community's Skate 3 engine rewrite. Works on any map (grind rails are found automatically) with any playermodel. Equip the Skateboard and you're riding.

[b]Free forever.[/b] Unofficial fan project, not affiliated with EA or Facepunch.

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Skate 3's physics and trick system, driven from a controller like the real thing.
[*]Your own playermodel rides the board, posed by Skate 3's animations, and other players see you skate.
[*]Skate 3's own sound engine (beta), ported from becaring/SK8V and fed from your disc: pops and landings by surface, grind and wheel loops, seam clicks, bails and the real x2/x3 chimes. The older Skate 3 sounds (or Half-Life 2's) are the fallback.
[*]Skate 3's HUD and menus: score, LINE, trick stack, FAKIE, the Hall of Meat bail panel, and the L1 quick menu (session marker, Interact, games).
[*]Seven skatepark maps (gm_skate3_*) built from your disc, plus tool gun placement for park pieces.
[*]Skaters hit each other: crashes, punches and board smacks (B / R1). Spawned props you don't freeze can be skated too.
[*]Trick score in three styles: minimal, floating beside you, or Half-Life 2.
[*]Session markers, like Skate 3. Bail damage can be switched off by the server.
[*]The [b]Skate 3 Surface[/b] tool (tool gun, Skate 3 tab) fixes a map's collision for skating: flatten a bumpy floor, smooth a ramp, ignore clutter, draw a grind rail, or make a ramp prop use its visible shape. Flags are saved per map and can be shared as a file.
[/list]

[h2]What you need[/h2]
[list]
[*]Your own copy of Skate 3 for Xbox 360, as a disc image (.iso). Nothing from the game ships here; the setup reads what the mod needs from your disc on your own computer.
[*]64-bit Garry's Mod: Steam → Garry's Mod → Properties → Betas → [b]x86-64[/b].
[*]Linux / SteamOS (native or Proton) or Windows. Not on macOS yet.
[*]A controller. On Steam Deck / SteamOS, Garry's Mod's controller layout must be a [b]Gamepad[/b] template, not keyboard and mouse.
[/list]

[h2]Install[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe to this addon.
[*]Get the S3GM setup from the [b]gmod-releases[/b] channel on [url=DISCORD_INVITE_LINK]Enxvinity's Atelier on Discord[/url]. The Workshop can't carry the skate engine itself, so it comes from there, like G64 does.
[*]Extract it into your Garry's Mod folder and run the setup once with your Skate 3 .iso. It finds Garry's Mod, installs the engine, and converts your disc's skater, animations and sounds. Run it again after an update. Leave "Skate 3's own sound engine" ticked (a few GB, a few more minutes).
[*]Load a map and equip [b]Skateboard[/b] (spawn menu → Weapons → Skate 3).
[/olist]

[h2]Controls[/h2]
Skate 3's own: [b]A[/b] pushes, [b]Y[/b] gets on and off the board, the right stick flicks tricks, triggers grab. [b]D-pad down[/b] drops a session marker, hold [b]D-pad up[/b] to go back to it. [b]B[/b] / [b]R1[/b] punches, or smacks with the board when it's in your hand. Switch weapons to leave skate mode.

[h2]Settings[/h2]
Spawn menu → Utilities → Skate 3: stance (regular or goofy), camera height, the sound engine switch with its status, volume, and the trick score's look. Server: [b]skate3_bail_damage[/b] turns bail damage on or off.

[h2]Known conflicts[/h2]
These addons together leaked memory until the game crashed during testing. If you see "CUtlRBTree overflow", try disabling them:
[list]
[*]First-person body ("Тело от Первого лица")
[*]Source Shadows
[*]InfMap base
[*]LIDAR
[*]Portal Gun (Lua rework)
[/list]

